  "rationale": "Every job repeatedly runs `poetry install --no-root` with no dependency cache, so dependency downloads are repeated across jobs and runs. The P-LIT-GHA-CACHE pattern (reviewed, reported benefit) supports caching dependency downloads keyed on the lockfile and environment, with modest measured VM-time reduction. Adding a `actions/cache@v4` step for `~/.cache/pypoetry`, keyed on `runner.os`, the Python version, and `poetry.lock`, before each `poetry install` preserves all build/test steps and coverage while reusing restored dependencies. No permissions are weakened, no secrets or deployment steps are added, and no existing check is removed or skipped.",
